WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:04.260
Working in a morgue requires some specific
skills.

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:07.130
You need to be comfortable being around the
dead.

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:09.219
You need to have a great attention to detail.

00:00:09.219 --> 00:00:14.030
And you’d better not be squeamish - you’ll
be getting up-close and personal with some

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:15.950
gruesome specimens.

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:21.380
But for those who find themselves in a specific
morgue under the supervision of the SCP foundation,

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:27.840
they’ll need to have some EXTRA specific
skills - if they hope to get out alive.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:31.600
In the basement of an old hospital in Great
Britain, there is a morgue.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:37.199
It appeared like any other until the 1980s,
with a busy hospital staff coming in and out

00:00:37.199 --> 00:00:42.320
to investigate causes of death and perform
autopsies, reporting anything unique to the

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:44.109
doctors upstairs.

00:00:44.109 --> 00:00:48.899
But soon, the morgue and the hospital around
it began to get a reputation.

00:00:48.899 --> 00:00:53.440
People whispered that something wasn’t right
in the morgue, that there were supernatural

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:55.230
dealings afoot.

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:58.010
And soon, they were proven right.

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:03.670
Because what’s dead in SCP-022 doesn’t
always stay dead.

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:08.310
The Foundation soon stepped in and quarantined
the morgue, condemning the building.

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:12.570
An investigation didn’t find any cause for
the unpredictable and dangerous phenomena,

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:18.210
but the Foundation was able to track the pattern
of reanimations - and did happen upon the

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:23.570
following: The morgue is filled with body
storage drawers and at random times, the spontaneous

00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:26.630
opening of one or several of them will occur.

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:31.829
And despite the fact that the morgue has been
out of operation for quite a long while, whenever

00:01:31.829 --> 00:01:37.540
a drawer opens, there is a body laying inside
under a sheet every time.

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:41.520
And after six minutes of being opened, the
body will wake up.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:46.590
When awake, these reanimated corpses have
exactly one mission - to get out of the morgue

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:48.979
by any means necessary.

00:01:48.979 --> 00:01:53.279
If the corpse is relatively intact, it will
leap off the table and charge at the door

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:55.950
- and anything else in its way.

00:01:55.950 --> 00:02:00.369
While no specimen has ever been safely captured
for testing, their base strength seems to

00:02:00.369 --> 00:02:03.270
be far stronger than any normal human.

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:08.210
No evidence of what gives them this power
has been found, but they are absolutely formidable

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:09.869
and very hard to stop.

00:02:09.869 --> 00:02:15.180
And to add to the difficulty...They’re even
harder to kill a second time around.

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:20.090
While all evidence indicates that these are
reanimated humans, they do not seem to be

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:23.370
limited by the same physical effects of damage.

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:27.150
Those who have tried to stop these undead
beings from getting to the door have found

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:28.959
this out the hard way.

00:02:28.959 --> 00:02:32.740
These cadavers seem to be immune to just about
any form of impairment.

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:38.060
Their bodies don’t give off heat, and they
do not need to eat, drink, or breathe.

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:43.069
If their bodies are severely damaged, the
body part with the greatest mass stays active

00:02:43.069 --> 00:02:45.750
and doesn’t seem to slow down at all.

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:50.230
Only one thing actually seems to impede upon
the horrifying persistence that these cadavers

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:53.620
portray in their attempts to escape… fire.

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:57.909
The Foundation has discovered that fire may
be the one effective way of stopping the undead

00:02:57.909 --> 00:03:02.860
specimens - but it’s not as easy as simply
setting them on fire.

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:06.739
High-powered fire is needed, to incinerate
their tissue and render them little more than

00:03:06.739 --> 00:03:08.379
a pile of ash.

00:03:08.379 --> 00:03:12.769
The good news is, there is another method
to neutralize them - and that’s to wait

00:03:12.769 --> 00:03:13.769
them out.

00:03:13.769 --> 00:03:18.490
If the corpse is active but contained by the
Foundation's security, they will eventually

00:03:18.490 --> 00:03:23.670
expire when whatever power is animating them
finally runs out - but this can take between

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:29.310
two days and three weeks, which can be problematic
if they’re joined by other friends from

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:30.560
the drawers.

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:34.319
But not all of the living corpses follow the
same pattern.

00:03:34.319 --> 00:03:38.780
Bodies emerge in the drawers seemingly at
random, and the state they arrive in is just

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:40.549
as unpredictable.

00:03:40.549 --> 00:03:45.439
This may correspond to how they died, and
an investigation is ongoing in regard to how

00:03:45.439 --> 00:03:48.310
these corpses wind up in the morgue to begin
with.

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:52.440
Some arrive in good shape, as if they were
recently deceased from a heart attack or other

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:54.010
similar ailment.

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:56.450
These are the most dangerous specimens.

00:03:56.450 --> 00:04:00.519
Others may be decomposed or damaged, which
will cause them to be slower.

00:04:00.519 --> 00:04:05.120
But some are in such poor condition that they
can’t get up off the slab at all.

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:09.659
And that’s where SCP-022 reacts in an unexpected
way.

00:04:09.659 --> 00:04:14.430
The cadaver may be too damaged to move, but
it’s still reanimated, and will struggle

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:19.019
and twitch on the slab for whatever the duration
is of their reanimated life.

00:04:19.019 --> 00:04:24.370
But if it expires while still on the slab,
the slab will act on its own, and slide back

00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:27.190
into the drawer with the cadaver still on
it.

00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:32.680
The body then disappears, and from what witnesses
have reported, a smell of burning tissue similar

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:35.889
to cremation then fills the air in the morgue.

00:04:35.889 --> 00:04:42.080
No one knows where the corpses go - but perhaps
more importantly, where do they come from?

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:47.070
That is the one question that concerns the
Foundation the most about SCP-022.

00:04:47.070 --> 00:04:51.590
While the main priority is to contain the
reanimated corpses, studying them is also

00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:52.590
vital.

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:57.530
Unfortunately, testing on the reanimated is
limited due to their aggressive nature, however,

00:04:57.530 --> 00:05:01.970
agents have been able to observe them just
enough to describe them and send the descriptions

00:05:01.970 --> 00:05:07.750
out to law enforcement, as evidence shows
that SCP-022 may also be able to reach outside

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:09.440
of the confines of the morgue.

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:14.210
What the Foundation has learned from interfacing
with local law enforcement, is that every

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:18.919
single one resembles a corpse stolen from
a morgue around the country.

00:05:18.919 --> 00:05:23.650
Studies of the specimens after they expire,
if not consumed by the drawers, is the easiest

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:25.250
way to conduct testing.

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:29.880
They can be examined safely and appear to
be standard human corpses with the only exception

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:33.790
being any damage done during the attempt by
the Foundation to contain them.

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:38.860
They don’t seem to have any unusual organs
or chemicals in the body, and no explanation

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:41.520
for their reanimation can be found.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:47.430
There is however, one other element of SCP-022
that concerns researchers.

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:50.130
Nothing seems to be able to be added to the
morgue.

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:55.690
When something is placed into or enters the
room, it vanishes after only seconds.

00:05:55.690 --> 00:06:00.500
This has happened to inanimate objects, as
well as to animals - and even to people.

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:04.340
There is no evidence as to where these specimens
go.

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:09.169
What makes this happen is unknown, but provides
further evidence for the theory that there

00:06:09.169 --> 00:06:16.210
is definitely some dangerous anomaly governing
SCP-022, far beyond the fact corpses are simply

00:06:16.210 --> 00:06:17.210
reanimating.

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:22.220
While the rest of the hospital that contains
SCP-022 has so far been free of anomalies

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:27.979
and is a standard abandoned building, an exploration
of the room above the morgue revealed something

00:06:27.979 --> 00:06:28.979
concerning.

00:06:28.979 --> 00:06:33.479
In the room, agents discovered a massive pile
of matter that seemed to be composed of all

00:06:33.479 --> 00:06:37.770
the things that had vanished upon entering
SCP-022.

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:43.599
All of the metal objects had been broken down,
and the organic material had decomposed.

00:06:43.599 --> 00:06:47.860
Everything looked like it had been there far
longer than the time since it had vanished,

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:51.949
despite appearing only three minutes after
its disappearance in testing.

00:06:51.949 --> 00:06:54.900
But one thing was missing from the mystery
pile.

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:59.370
What happened to the people who had disappeared
inside the morgue?

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:03.360
None of the humans who disappeared, either
in accidents before the Foundation stepped

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:07.960
in or in testing, appeared in the pile in
decayed form.

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:11.120
But it wasn’t long before they appeared
in another way.

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:15.190
The Foundation observed that several of the
corpses that appeared from behind the drawers

00:07:15.190 --> 00:07:21.670
of SCP-022 resembled the unfortunate citizens
who had disappeared into the room in the past.

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:25.039
The morgue’s victims had returned - and
they wanted out.

00:07:25.039 --> 00:07:29.240
Now it was clear that the priority had to
be containment.

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:34.229
The door to the facility was destroyed during
a security breach by a particularly tenacious

00:07:34.229 --> 00:07:38.640
specimen, so The Foundation installed a more
powerful vault door shortly after taking over

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:42.539
the facility, with orders that it must remain
locked at all times.

00:07:42.539 --> 00:07:46.720
Because of the morgue’s ability to absorb
anything that enters it, containment of the

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:50.650
entities is dependent entirely on automated
systems.

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:54.159
If the cadavers happen to make it through
the vault door placed just outside of the

00:07:54.159 --> 00:08:00.191
perimeter of the original SCP-022 room, awaiting
their arrival are the Foundation’s high-powered

00:08:00.191 --> 00:08:02.159
automated fire weapons.

00:08:02.159 --> 00:08:06.500
Once the undead cross the threshold of the
door, the weapons are triggered and incinerate

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:07.500
them immediately.

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:12.919
It is only if this system fails that response
teams are sent in to contain the threat, followed

00:08:12.919 --> 00:08:14.490
by cleanup crews.

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:20.180
No humans are to enter SCP-022 unless further
testing is needed, nor is any entity to be

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:22.620
removed from the containment site.

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:26.740
While the first time the Foundation encountered
one of the reanimated corpses it had been

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:31.020
immediately destroyed, the second time was
a different story.

00:08:31.020 --> 00:08:36.210
It appeared to be an Asian man in his fifties,
and its body was mostly intact with the exception

00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:39.760
of a large chest scar that resembled that
of an autopsy.

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:45.100
It claimed its name was John, and remembered
dying in a car accident - but it refused to

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:46.560
admit that it was dead.

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:51.340
Then it saw its reflection, and things took
a disturbing turn.

00:08:51.340 --> 00:08:55.590
While the specimen had remained calm until
then, it became extremely angry as soon as

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:58.840
it saw its image on the steel table and had
to be restrained.

00:08:58.840 --> 00:09:03.660
While in containment, it claimed over and
over again that it was not the man it saw

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:04.660
in it’s reflection.

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:08.230
Whoever was in the body, didn't believe it
was the older Asian man.

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:13.960
It then became enraged, screaming and smashing
its head against a wall until it stopped talking

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:16.610
and eventually stopped moving all together.

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:19.080
No more information could be obtained.

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:22.940
What was SCP-022 doing to the people who appeared
in it?

00:09:22.940 --> 00:09:26.980
The answer to that question became a little
clearer after the Foundation was able to capture

00:09:26.980 --> 00:09:28.550
a specimen again.

00:09:28.550 --> 00:09:35.400
This time it was shortly after a D-class designated
D-5619 had been sent into the morgue and immediately

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:36.400
disappeared.

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:40.520
What emerged from the drawer shortly thereafter,
though, wasn’t the D-class.

00:09:40.520 --> 00:09:44.040
It was a little girl who looked to be about
twelve years old.

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:48.630
And just like the cadaver captured prior,
when restrained, it became extremely angry.

00:09:48.630 --> 00:09:52.880
However, it did eventually cooperate in answering
questions for the Foundation.

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:59.110
It was soon identified as D-5619, the unfortunate
D-class testing victim.

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:04.640
It wasn’t long after that the question of
what happened to D-5619’s body was answered.

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:10.800
Three weeks following the incident, D-5619’s
body returned from the drawers - but it wasn’t

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:12.310
him inside of it.

00:10:12.310 --> 00:10:17.210
A brief interview confirmed that this was
a very confused but overall cooperative 89-year-old

00:10:17.210 --> 00:10:19.600
woman in the body of the D-class.

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:25.880
Whatever effect is going on within SCP-022,
it seems to return people in twisted, mismatched

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:28.340
combinations of body and mind.

00:10:28.340 --> 00:10:34.221
The Foundation is still investigating exactly
what is happening inside of SCP-022, with

00:10:34.221 --> 00:10:37.980
a focus on how the anomaly gets its corpses
from around Great Britain.

00:10:37.980 --> 00:10:43.830
But when dealing with the mystery morgue itself,
the Foundation holds to a simple rule.

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:47.080
Nothing gets in - and nothing gets out.

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:53.290
For more on a mysterious threat in an unlikely
place, check out “SCP-974 - Treehouse Predator”,

00:10:53.290 --> 00:10:56.940
or check out this other video instead for
more from SCP Explained.

